+# Setup Passport: gothinkster/node-express-realworld-example-app
+
+✅ **VERIFIED**: HUMBLE followed this project's setup docs on a clean `node:22` machine, repaired what broke, then replayed the corrected guide from zero.
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Commit | `30b68e1e88` |
+| Verified | 2026-09-27 07:59 UTC |
+| Runtime | Node.js 22 (`node:22`) |
+| Clone to running, from zero | **1m03s** |
+| Steps followed | 4 from the docs, 1 added by HUMBLE |
+| Breaks found / fixed | 2 / 2 |
+| Needs a human | 0 |
+| Done when | every step exits cleanly |
+| IBM Bob | 1 diagnosis, 1.96 Bobcoins |
+
+**Before HUMBLE**, a newcomer following the docs got stuck at `npx prisma migrate deploy` (README.md:46).
+
+## Verified setup
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npx prisma generate
+export DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
+npx prisma migrate deploy
+npx prisma db seed
+```
+
+## Evidence
+
+Every change to the docs is backed by a command that failed before the fix and passed after it.
+
+### E1: Undocumented environment variable <a id="e1"></a>
+
+- **Docs said:** `npx prisma migrate deploy` (README.md:46)
+- **Cause:** The app requires DATABASE_URL at startup, but the docs never mention it.
+- **Diagnosed by:** HUMBLE rule `missing-env-var`, confidence 90%
+- **Doc change:** export DATABASE_URL=…
+- **Result:** fixed and verified
+
+<details><summary>Before (failing output)</summary>
+
+```
+
+Error: Prisma schema validation - (get-config wasm)
+Error code: P1012
+error: Environment variable not found: DATABASE_URL.
+  -->  schema.prisma:3
+   | 
+ 2 |   provider = "postgresql"
+ 3 |   url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
+   | 
+
+Validation Error Count: 1
+[Context: getConfig]
+
+Prisma CLI Version : 4.16.2
+```
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>Fix applied</summary>
+
+```
+$ export DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres → exit 0
+```
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>After (passing output)</summary>
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  Update available 4.16.2 -> 8.0.0-rc.17                 │
+│                                                         │
+│  This is a major update - please follow the guide at    │
+│  https://pris.ly/d/major-version-upgrade                │
+│                                                         │
+│  Run the following to update                            │
+│    npm i --save-dev prisma@latest                       │
+│    npm i @prisma/client@latest                          │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+</details>
+
+### E2: Undocumented backing service <a id="e2"></a>
+
+- **Docs said:** `npx prisma migrate deploy` (README.md:46)
+- **Cause:** README.md line 46 runs `npx prisma migrate deploy` without ever starting a PostgreSQL server; the error `P1001: Can't reach database server at localhost:5432` proves no database is running.
+- **Diagnosed by:** IBM Bob (0.047774 Bobcoins), confidence 99%
+- **Doc change:** Before running `npx prisma migrate deploy`, start a PostgreSQL instance (e.g. `docker run -d -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres -p 5432:5432 postgres:16-alpine`) and set DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres.
+- **Result:** fixed and verified
+
+<details><summary>Before (failing output)</summary>
+
+```
+Prisma schema loaded from src/prisma/schema.prisma
+Datasource "db": PostgreSQL database "postgres", schema "public" at "localhost:5432"
+
+Error: P1001: Can't reach database server at `localhost`:`5432`
+
+Please make sure your database server is running at `localhost`:`5432`.
+```
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>Fix applied</summary>
+
+```
+started postgres:16-alpine as "postgres" on localhost:5432
+```
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>After (passing output)</summary>
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  Update available 4.16.2 -> 8.0.0-rc.17                 │
+│                                                         │
+│  This is a major update - please follow the guide at    │
+│  https://pris.ly/d/major-version-upgrade                │
+│                                                         │
+│  Run the following to update                            │
+│    npm i --save-dev prisma@latest                       │
+│    npm i @prisma/client@latest                          │
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+```
+</details>
+
+## Keeping it true
+
+The workflow in `.github/workflows/firstrun.yml` re-checks setup on every pull request that touches the README, manifests, env files or compose files, and comments when a change would break a newcomer's first run.
